# Summary
Introduced a new external WhatsApp-to-RAG path that fails to enforce knowledge document visibility before constructing a bot reply. The underlying visibility field existed already, but this commit exposes it to end users through the new orchestrator.
The commit adds automatic RAG replies for inbound WhatsApp messages. The retrieval query only restricts by tenant and active status, but does not exclude documents whose visibility is agents_only. Because build_grounded_answer returns an answer containing an excerpt of the best chunk, any WhatsApp contact can ask a matching question and receive content from agent-only knowledge documents. This violates the documented RAG visibility boundary for end-user responses and can disclose internal policies, escalation instructions, discounts, operational notes, or other staff-only tenant data.

